1. LEMON network simplex (as adapted by Nicolas Bonneel)
--------------------------------------------------------

Files:
  src/network_simplex_simple.h
  src/full_bipartitegraph.h

Origin:
  network_simplex.h and full_graph.h from LEMON, a generic C++ optimization
  library (https://lemon.cs.elte.hu/), adapted by Nicolas Bonneel (2013) into
  a lightweight network simplex for mass transport. Bonneel's revisions
  (listed in the file headers): OpenMP parallelisation (March 2015), a
  robustness fix by Antoine Rolet (March 2017), and a bug fix with 64-bit
  integers, an updated algorithm and sparse flows (April 2018). The same
  adaptation is distributed with the Python Optimal Transport (POT) library.
  A previous version is part of the Displacement Interpolation project:
  http://www.cs.ubc.ca/labs/imager/tr/2011/DisplacementInterpolation/

